{"blocks":[["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-23822","Second choice: Proposal C",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Recommended core decision"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-23856","An OCaml/mldoc-based core, if the compatibility experiment exposes important lsdoc gaps.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Recommended core decision","Second choice: Proposal C"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-23954","The case for C is stronger than \"OCaml is good at parsers.\" Current mldoc actually has a dedicated Logseq indexing-like fast path: parse_outline_only, and md_outline.ml says directly that it is line-oriented and avoids the more expensive Angstrom choice/backtracking hot path while preserving Logseq-relevant outline material. That makes C a technically serious alternative, not merely a conservative fallback.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Recommended core decision","Second choice: Proposal C"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-24376","Proposal A as UI spike only",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Recommended core decision"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-24412","A Marksman + tiny blink.cmp source + simple index can prove that double-bracket wiki-link completion in LazyVim feels right. It should not become the long-term architecture because the moment agents, backlinks, block refs and the publisher need the same data, putting indexing logic inside the Neovim side becomes duplicated work. That is precisely the problem the shared semantic engine in the Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Brief is designed to avoid.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Recommended core decision","Proposal A as UI spike only"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-24895","Treat A as an optional one-evening vertical slice, not as an alternative product architecture.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Recommended core decision","Proposal A as UI spike only"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-24995","Also, consistent with the note in the Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Proposal/Fable proposal, do not make upstream collaboration part of the initial plan. Pin commits, create local forks or vendor code where licensing permits, learn from six months of real use, and only then decide whether any upstream relationship is strategically desirable.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Recommended core decision"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-25364","Architecture comparison",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-25394","Compatibility oracle",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Architecture comparison"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-25423","mldoc + Logseq/OG graph-parser + graph-validator",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Architecture comparison","Compatibility oracle"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-25485","Shared input",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Architecture comparison"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-25506","Logseq/OG garden: pages/ · journals/ · assets/ · logseq/",["Logseq